<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Trần Trọng Kim</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1883–1953</span> · Also known as Tran Trong Kim</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Trần Trọng Kim (1883–1953) was a Vietnamese scholar and historian, author of a widely read outline history of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>, who served as prime minister of the Japanese-backed Empire of Vietnam from April to August 1945. His government ended when Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bao-dai">Bảo Đại</a> abdicated during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/august-revolution">August Revolution</a> led by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viet-minh">Viet Minh</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tran-trong-kim.jpg" alt="Trần Trọng Kim" width="320" height="426" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mr._Tran_Trong_Kim.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
